---
title: 'High-Frequency Data'
description: 'Efficiently update $framework chart data using the applyTransaction() API for real-time and streaming scenarios.'
---

Efficiently update chart data in real-time scenarios using incremental transactions.

High-frequency data updates occur when charts need to reflect rapidly changing data, such as live financial tickers, IoT sensor readings, or real-time analytics dashboards. The `applyTransaction()` API provides high-performance incremental updates that are 90%+ faster than full data replacement for small changes.

## Apply Transaction API

The `applyTransaction()` method allows efficient incremental updates to chart data without replacing the entire dataset.

{% apiReference id="_AgChartInstanceInterface" include=["applyTransaction"] hideHeader=true hideRequired=true /%}

{% if isFramework("react") %}
The `AgChartInstance` can be obtained using a React `Ref` to our `<AgCharts />` tag, which
exposes a `chart` property.
{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("angular") %}
The `AgChartInstance` can be obtained using an Angular `@ViewChild` decorator to reference our `AgCharts` tag, which
exposes a `chart` property.
{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("vue") %}
The `AgChartInstance` can be obtained using the Vue `$refs` component property to reference our `AgCharts` tag, which
exposes a `chart` property.
{% /if %}

